2: 
3: A job declares what it takes; `small run` passes it; the script reads it; whatever it
4: writes to an output directory is captured on the run.
5: 
6: Schema in `small.toml`:
7: 
8: ```toml
9: [inputs]
10: image     = { type = "file",   required = true, accept = ".jpg,.png", help = "Photo to analyse" }
11: threshold = { type = "number", default = 0.5, min = 0, max = 1 }
12: account   = { type = "select", options = ["acme", "globex"] }
13: since     = { type = "date",   default = "-7d" }
14: label     = { type = "text",   pattern = "^[a-z0-9-]*$" }
15: dry_run   = { type = "bool",   default = false }
16: 
17: [outputs]
18: report = { path = "report.pdf", label = "Weekly report" }
19: ```
20: 
21: Exactly six types: `file`, `number`, `select`, `date`, `text`, `bool`. Anything else is
22: rejected at `small init` and `small deploy` with a one-line error.
23: 
24: ## CLI (implemented)
25: 
26: `small run <app> --image ./photo.jpg --threshold 0.7 --dry-run`. One flag per input
27: (underscores become dashes: `dry_run` → `--dry-run`), validated against the schema before
28: anything is uploaded: required present, number in range, select in options, file extension
29: in `accept`, text matches `pattern`. Relative dates (`-7d`) resolve to `YYYY-MM-DD` at
30: validation so the script gets a concrete date. The schema is read from the local
31: `small.toml`; passing input flags without one is an error.
32: 
33: Validated inputs print before the run starts:
34: 
35: ```
36: ✓ inputs: image=photo.jpg (48 KB) · threshold=0.7 · dry_run=true
37: ```
38: 
39: Input files are capped at 100 MB total per run, checked before upload. After the run
40: finishes the CLI lists output files with sizes and the fetch command:
41: 
42: ```
43: outputs:
44:   annotated.jpg  214 KB
45:   boxes.json     2 KB
46: fetch: small run yolo-job --download ./out
47: ```
48: 
49: `small run <app> --download ./out` downloads every output of the latest finished run.
50: 
51: ## Wire contract (for the control-plane and runtime halves)
52: 
53: - `POST /api/runs` — unchanged JSON `{ app, inputs?: { name: value } }` when there are no
54:   file inputs. With files: multipart form with field `body` holding that same JSON string,
55:   plus one file part per file input named `input:<name>` (original filename preserved).
56:   File inputs appear in `inputs` as their original filename string.
57: - Inputs are stored on the run row as JSON. Uploaded files go to R2 keyed by run id.
58: - `GET /api/runs/<id>/outputs` → `{ outputs: [{ name, size }] }`
59: - `GET /api/runs/<id>/outputs/<name>` → the file bytes.
60: - Uploads capped at 100 MB per run.
61: 
62: ## Runtime (pending — separate change)
63: 
64: `runner.py` receives inputs and writes: scalars as `SMALL_INPUT_<NAME>` env vars
65: (uppercase), files to `$SMALL_INPUTS/<name><ext>`, and everything to
66: `$SMALL_INPUTS/inputs.json`. Creates `$SMALL_OUTPUTS/`. On exit, uploads every file in it
67: to the control plane, declared or not.
68: 
69: ## Control plane (pending — separate change)
70: 
71: Run-row inputs JSON, R2 storage, the two outputs routes, the 100 MB cap.
72: 
73: ## Example (pending — separate change)
74: 
75: `examples/yolo-job` from `examples/yolo-gradio`: takes `image` and `threshold`, writes
76: `annotated.jpg` and `boxes.json` to `$SMALL_OUTPUTS`. The Gradio one stays.
77: 
78: ## Skill (pending — separate change)
79: 
80: SKILL.md: every non-secret `os.environ` read in a job is an input — declare it. Anything
81: the script saves for the user goes in `$SMALL_OUTPUTS`.
82: 
83: ## Skipped
84: 
85: - Web run form — ponytail: the CLI flags cover job runs; form belongs to the dashboard work.
86: - Multiple selects — ponytail: single select covers the known apps; add `multiple = true` when one needs it.
87: - Outputs over 100 MB — ponytail: flat cap; raise or stream to R2 multipart when a real job hits it.
